=== STEP 5 RESULT: Recipe 3 Custom Widget Implementation Template ===

To implement a custom interactive control (checkbox, slider, radio, custom chart), follow this pattern:

### Phase 1: State Definition (Define minimal state shape)
  - Simplest possible state (one boolean for checkbox, one usize for segmented, etc.)
  - State shape guides implementation strategy
  - Tests write state shape before code

### Phase 2: Element Tree Construction (Build from primitives)
  - Draw from state parameter (upvalue, not closure)
  - Conditional styling (state determines appearance)
  - Handler receives &mut S directly
  - Built from primitives (no special framework magic)

### Phase 3: Enhancement (Styling & Visual Polish)
  - Focus ring, hover highlight, disabled state
  - Platform-appropriate styling (rounded corners, badges, etc.)
  - Contrast validation (text ≥7, secondary ≥4.5)
  - Dark/light mode testing

### Phase 4: Integration & Persistence (Multi-instance state management)
  - Multiple instances coexist with independent state
  - State persists across frames (memory.rs, path-based identity)
  - Reordered lists preserve state via .key()
  - Integration tests (10+ frames, state mutation tracking)

### Verification Checklist
  ✓ State shape defined and tested
  ✓ Element tree built from primitives (draw, row, col, on_click)
  ✓ Conditional styling proof (state determines appearance)
  ✓ Focus ring, hover, disabled states working
  ✓ Multiple instances with independent state verified
  ✓ State persists across 10+ frames (memory.rs confirms)
  ✓ Reordered lists preserve state via .key()
  ✓ All tests passing (no regressions)

